// ISO 23726-3 (IDO) 4.2: the graph model and sample data
//
// Generated by ../../cypher.py from model.json and sample.json. Edit those and regenerate, rather than this file.
//
// Condensate export pump P-2001A at the fictional Nordvik gas terminal. The export system's two pump functions (duty
// P-2001A and standby P-2001B) are implemented by physical pumps, serial numbers 48213 and 48214, installed in
// process module 20. The installed pump has assembled parts, a duplex stainless steel casing and rated and measured
// quantities with their units on its datasheet. Its installation, timed by start and end events, is followed by a
// mechanical seal replacement whose performance test realises the pumping function.
//
// Run it against an empty database of Neo4j 5 or later, Enterprise Edition, for its node key and property existence
// constraints, e.g. with cypher-shell -f model.cypher. It merges every node and relationship, so it can be run again.

// The model: its constraints

